    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This plugin enables <a href=\"https://yogobooking.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">YOGO</a> integration on your WordPress website.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.yogo.dk/da/articles/6620472-integration-med-wordpress\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Official documentation</a></p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Activate the plugin.</li>\n<li>Go to the YOGO Booking settings page and enter your YOGO domain. It will look something like <code>mystudio.yogobooking.com</code>.</li>\n<li>Try typing <code>[yogo-calendar]</code> on one of your pages. It should show the schedule for your studio.</li>\n<li>If nothing happens, check that you entered your domain correctly.</li>\n<li>You&#8217;re done!</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"is%20this%20a%20booking%20system%3F\">\nIs this a booking system?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p><a href=\"https://yogobooking.com\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">YOGO</a> is a booking system. This plugin makes it easy to embed your schedule, price list, events, teacher list and more into your WordPress website.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"do%20i%20need%20an%20account%20with%20yogo%20to%20use%20this%20plugin%3F\">\nDo I need an account with YOGO to use this plugin?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>The plugin itself is free and open source, but you will not have any use for it without a YOGO account.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"what%20data%20does%20the%20plugin%20send%20to%20yogo%3F\">\nWhat data does the plugin send to YOGO?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>As part of the service connection, the plugin reports its own status to YOGO: plugin version, chosen settings, your YOGO domain, and your WordPress/PHP versions. It never sends any visitor or customer data.</p>\n</p>\n\n"
    },
